WEBVTT

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:07.130
<i>In regards to these unexpected events,</i>
<i>as I'm sure you all understand,</i>

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:09.960
<i>we must bring the situation</i>
<i>under control as soon as possible</i>

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.720
<i>and secure the safety</i>
<i>of the disaster victims.</i>

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:16.180
I, the Prime Minister
of the Provisional Shibuya Government,

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.810
Seiichiro Muta,
as head of this administration,

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.890
have decided to cooperate with
the Revisions, the people of the future

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.520
after intense deliberation.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.560
You're kidding!

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.650
-With the Revisions?
-Seriously?

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:31.610
Cooperate? Aren't they the enemy?

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.240
When did they decide this?

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.820
I was told last night.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.370
It seems the Revisions
made direct contact.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:43.620
Because of this,
we can now negotiate with them

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.960
about sending all
the Shibuya disaster victims

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.250
back to their original time,
the year 2017!

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.800
That's wonderful!

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.930
If you succeed, Mayor Muta,

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:57.090
your name will go down in history!

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.600
There is no way they will negotiate!

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.180
You'll just end up being used by them!
You must believe in the AHRV!

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:07.810
Ms. Milo. You are a person of the future
as well, aren't you?

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:10.940
The people of our time
will make our own decisions!

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:14.990
Besides, you have no evidence
that would allow us to believe you.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.070
That's right!

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.660
Are you going to return us to our time?

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.370
Additionally,

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:26.000
as part of the deal, we will hand over
the Anti-Revisions Wearable Combat System,

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.630
the String Puppets, to the Revisions.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:29.670
Then,

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:33.960
we will begin the process, starting
with the first repatriation group.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:35.130
That's incredible!

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.550
For the First Repatriation...

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.720
Congratulations, Mr. Keisaku Asano.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:42.810
You will be returning with your mother.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:43.930
What?

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:47.770
To ensure that there are second
and third groups until everyone returns,

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:52.520
we, the Provisional Shibuya Government,
will carry out negotiations responsibly.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.150
Isn't it great, Keisaku?

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:56.900
What? Oh, yes.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:35.500
Yes!

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.130
Yes! My name is up there!

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.090
You've got to be kidding? Where's my name?

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.840
Your name and your mom's are on the list.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:42.930
I guess so.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:44.470
This is pretty unusual.

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:48.560
I mean, I have crazy bad luck, you see.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.520
-What do you mean?
-But I think I'm going to pass this time.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:55.400
-I'll have my mom go back first--
-Don't be fooled!

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.610
They killed us humans!
Negotiating with them is useless!

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.070
We'll all be killed!

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:04.200
They're demanding
we give them the String Puppets!

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.160
That means disarming ourselves!

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.370
We can't let our weapons go!

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.040
If you leave it to me,
I can kill them all!

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.330
I can save everyone!

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:15.170
-Listen--
-Down with war!

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.040
-Who said that?
-Buzz off, kid!

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:19.590
-Idiot!
-Who are you calling "idiot," you idiot?

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:22.220
You should believe me and Milo!

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.260
He never learns, does he?

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:32.270
All the Shibuya Defense Service ended up
doing was retrieving these things.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:34.440
But is this really a good idea?

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:35.770
No, it's not.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:39.320
How can we believe the Revisions
and put ourselves in their hands?

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.820
I'm sure they have an ulterior motive.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.360
What's wrong with all of them?

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.490
All they did was complain!

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:50.620
Who do they think protected them?

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:52.330
Damn it!

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.670
Oh, dear! There's nothing good
in this vacation!

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:03.050
The people of 2017 are so violent.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.220
Nice to meet you, person of the past.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.550
Let me introduce myself.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.430
My last name is Nico. I belong to Laos.
My first name is Sugar.

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:14.480
I think maybe I should call myself
Nicholas Sato in this time.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:17.100
What? A dog? A robot?

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:21.980
This form is just a temporary one called
a remote communication body, young man.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.070
-Communication...
-What do you think of my face?

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:27.820
I chose a form that would make it easier
for you to empathize with.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.030
So, you're a person of the future?

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.910
The future? Yes, that's right!

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:36.960
I am a member of the Revisions, you know.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.880
Damn you!

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:40.920
Listen.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:46.220
We, the Revisions, are offering
to return you to the year 2017.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:48.390
And yet you guys--

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:51.430
What?
So you're saying you brought us here?

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:52.600
That's right.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:57.020
But it's for the purpose
of saving mankind.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.190
What?

00:05:58.270 --> 00:05:59.600
Oh, you haven't heard?

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:03.070
You must be at the bottom
of the ladder, young man!

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.030
Well, then...

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:06.400
Farewell!

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.570
Jeez, what a waste of time.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:14.160
-Why, you! Release me!
-Tons of people have died because of you!

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.250
And you--

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:17.750
Sorry about that. I apologize.
My sincerest regrets.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:20.920
There were some in our group
that acted on their own.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.840
I'm not going to fall for that!

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.960
In any case, we're on your side.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:28.550
-Won't you believe me, young man?
-I will only believe Milo!

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:31.850
No matter what you plan
to use those monsters for,

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.760
I'm going to protect everyone!

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:34.850
I see!

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.640
So, this Milo is the agent from AHRV?

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.600
I see.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:42.270
In that case, young man,

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.110
do you know what AHRV's weapon is?

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.320
Man, I'm so lucky today!

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.280
This vacation's getting better!

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.740
Let's get to know each other!

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:58.580
I'm the lucky one!
I'm going to capture you--

00:06:58.660 --> 00:06:59.500
Pointless!

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:01.580
More importantly, don't forget!

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:04.290
We are on your side!

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.960
Milo and ARHV are the enemies!

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.550
You got that, young man?

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:09.550
Later!

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.260
Milo is the enemy?

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:19.140
<i>Let me ask you again.</i>

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:20.190
INTERROGATION ROOM 1

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.100
<i>What kind of organization is AHRV?</i>

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.440
Anti-Historical Revisionism.

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:27.570
It's an organization
to stop the Revision's selfish slaughter

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:29.570
and protect the existence of humanity.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.780
Where are your colleagues?

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.530
It's a secret. I can't tell you.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:36.370
Who are the Revisions?

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:41.040
They wouldn't hesitate to kill
their own family to save themselves.

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:42.170
They're monsters!

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:43.080
Listen.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:46.000
I see your desperate efforts
on our behalf.

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:48.090
It makes me want to believe you.

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:52.840
So, please,
will you trust us, the police, as well?

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:01.350
To begin with,
is it true that this is 2388?

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:04.850
There's no doubt about it.
You can run geological tests to prove it.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:08.150
How is it possible to leap time?

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:11.700
-It's a time jump by the quantum brain.
-What?

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:16.280
We at AHRV see time as a single string.

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:21.250
It's a string with complex turns
with multiple intersections.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:23.580
It's called the Chaotic Orbit.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:24.620
And?

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:27.630
These points where time crosses
are ambiguous,

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:30.300
meaning two different times
can exist at once.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:33.300
I don't really understand it, but...

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:36.550
Front or back, which do you see?

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.300
Both.

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:40.600
This is the current state of Shibuya.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:44.390
It's both the year 2388 and 2017 as well.

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:47.360
So, it's also 2017 right now?

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:48.520
That's right.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:51.530
But in order to perceive
and interact with this,

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:53.860
you need what's called a "quantum brain."

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:58.660
The agents known as "Balancers," like me,
are born with this brain.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:00.790
Do the Revisions have it too?

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:05.120
Only the AHRV can perceive the fragments
of the ideas of Platonism.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:08.290
They most likely
developed it artificially.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:12.170
They used it
to forcibly establish this state

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:14.340
with a method called "observation."

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:17.470
Sorry, this is completely over my head.

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:23.020
Our basic knowledge and concepts
are different. It can't be helped.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:26.520
Most likely, the transportation of Shibuya
hasn't been stabilized.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:29.730
If whatever is forcibly securing
this state disappears...

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:32.110
What if we destroy
the enemy's quantum brain?

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:37.410
We should be able to return Shibuya and
its people back to their previous state.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:39.030
But our predictions...

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:41.080
I cannot allow this.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:42.200
Is there a problem?

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:45.710
She's in a very delicate position,
you see.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:46.660
What?

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.040
I've been contacted by the Revisions.

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:52.460
We were told to be careful
of the AHRV agent.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.010
You're violating the firearms control law.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:58.970
"This is a crisis."
Wasn't it you who said that?

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:01.640
It doesn't mean you can exercise
a dictatorship, Mayor.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:03.390
You mean, "Prime Minister."

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:06.270
I mean, you'd like to return too,
wouldn't you?

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:09.850
There's no point in us, people
of the present, fighting among ourselves.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:11.270
Understood.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:18.820
Don't worry.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:21.030
We won't do anything rough.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.370
You're an important hostage, after all.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:31.290
Keisaku!

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:32.210
Mom!

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:36.670
I made rice balls for the soup kitchen.
I brought a few of them. Eat up.

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:40.720
Mom, I...

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:41.800
What is it?

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.760
Well, I...

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.850
I'm thinking of staying this time around.

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:50.440
I was thinking you could
go home first and wait for me--

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:52.020
Don't be a fool!

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:55.280
I can't leave my child here alone!

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:56.690
I won't allow it!

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:57.900
Yoshie!

00:10:58.190 --> 00:10:59.320
Coming!

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.780
Keisaku, eat the rice balls.
They're delicious.

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:03.070
Mom!

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:06.450
What should I do?

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:13.380
Daisuke, early morning tomorrow
the first repatriation will start.

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:14.380
I see.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.750
I'll be leaving you behind--

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.170
Mikio!

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:24.470
I still have things I need to do.

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:28.140
I have to protect everyone
until they all return.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:31.310
"The time will come
when I have to protect everyone."

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:32.270
Right.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.520
But that robot will be taken away.

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:35.900
I won't accept that.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.440
I won't let it happen.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:41.320
With the String Puppet's powers,
my powers, I'm going to kill them all!

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.240
Daisuke.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:45.030
If you do that without anyone asking,

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:47.870
-that's just violence.
-This is the right thing!

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.460
Throw down your weapons!

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:51.870
Hail the Revisions!

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:00.590
Deputy Mayor!

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:03.550
I would like to ask you a question.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:08.770
Mukyu.

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:10.640
You're late.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:13.190
Any changes to the probability
of Shibuya's existence?

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:17.360
Still 50 percent.
I keep on checking though.

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:20.990
I guess interacting
with just one time period doesn't work.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:25.160
But we're almost finished
with gathering the materials we need

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:28.660
to reincarnate Chiharu in a real body
with a quantum brain.

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:31.290
That may be true, but time is limited.

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:37.210
The crossing of the years 2388 and 2017
will eventually end.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.460
We must gather the materials before that.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:44.550
We may not succeed, and even if we do,
the lifespan could be short.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:48.810
Even so, I'm a little jealous
that Chiharu will have a real body.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:52.310
I want to hurry and part ways
with this incomplete body.

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:55.480
The materials this time are from humans
before the pandemic.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:58.020
-The chance of success should be high.
-Yes.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:03.740
Our plan will become the first page
of our brethren's history.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:05.660
-Speaking of which...
-What?

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:09.660
Is using that form really effective?

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:14.830
I think a smiling and stylish form
like mine is more appropriate.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:18.460
A suggestion from the lowly.
What do you think, Mukyu?

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:22.880
Who cares?
Who understands what ancient people think?

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.190
You're too obvious.

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:41.520
-Think about it. What can you do alone?
-I'm going to get the String Puppets back.

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:45.320
What if they kill the returnees
if you take the String Puppets?

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:49.450
Calm down. You think the Revisions
are suspicious too, right, Gai?

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:50.740
-Well, yes.
-Right?

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:52.370
Then what should we do?

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:55.540
It seems to me
like they're sorting the humans.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:59.080
So there are certain people
they don't want dead?

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:02.000
Yes, they may be collecting
only the people they need.

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:04.170
Seriously?
My mom and I are included in that.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:05.340
My uncle, too.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:07.340
Gai's theory is correct.

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:08.800
Mr. Kuroiwa.

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:10.930
The Deputy Mayor admitted it.

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:14.270
The repatriation list was provided
by the Revisions.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:17.890
There is no first or second group.
That's all there is.

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:20.190
Muta's name was on the list, too.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:21.360
I knew it!

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:26.070
Chances are high that those left
in Shibuya are disposable.

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:28.910
It makes sense that
they would take the String Puppets too,

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:30.780
so we can't resist.

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:33.370
So...

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:38.500
We will now begin our operation
to stop the first repatriation,

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:40.040
secure the returnees,

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.420
and retrieve the String Puppets!

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:43.670
Hold on. What about Milo?

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.340
She's in the interrogation room.

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:47.470
I've asked Izumi to check on her.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:51.590
First, Daisuke and Lu will work
on retrieving the String Puppets.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:54.680
<i>Before the Repatriation begins</i>
<i>in the morning at 11 a.m.,</i>

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:57.350
<i>sneak onto the transport trucks</i>
<i>carrying the String Puppets.</i>

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:58.680
<i>Izumi will help you.</i>

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:00.600
This is like a movie.

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:02.060
I'm nervous.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.730
Once Muta makes contact
with the Revisions,

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:07.400
depending on what's negotiated,
we'll activate the String Puppets,

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:09.530
secure Muta, and clean out the Revisions.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:12.160
We will secure the safety
of the returnees.

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:13.120
-Got it.
-Okay.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:14.580
Keisaku and Temari.

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:15.490
-Yes!
-Yes!

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:17.160
Me?

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:19.660
You will come with us.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:23.170
It's possible you will need
to pilot the String Puppets.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:25.040
But I've never been in one.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:27.840
Don't worry. We're just backup.

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:29.670
Ms. Milo is...

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:32.840
Prime Minister Muta said they're
handing over Milo to the Revisions.

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:33.970
-What?
-They want to

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.760
make a good impression with the Revisions.

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:37.310
I'll go save her!

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:38.470
Not that again.

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:39.600
No, wait.

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:41.940
If something happens to Milo,

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:45.570
we wouldn't even be here right now.

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:47.570
-You're right.
<i>-</i>What do you mean?

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:50.820
<i>We were caught up</i>
<i>in a kidnapping in the past.</i>

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:52.820
<i>Milo saved us.</i>

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:55.240
But Milo doesn't know of that incident.

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:57.660
It's probably Milo
from farther into the future that--

00:15:57.740 --> 00:15:59.290
This is too complicated!

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:02.080
Daisuke! Can I entrust Milo to you?

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:05.380
-Of course!
-Temari will pilot the String Puppet!

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:11.880
What a stubborn woman!

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:14.260
She never said a word about AHRV.

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:17.680
It's almost time. Let's start moving.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:20.060
We're handing her over anyway,

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:22.560
so why don't we have a little fun, right?

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:24.150
You'd better not.

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:32.900
<i>Daisuke, just don't do anything stupid.</i>

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:35.820
Thank you for your hard work, guys.

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:37.030
I brought snacks.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:38.830
-That's great.
-I'm starving!

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:42.000
-There's enough for everyone.
-So many options.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:44.370
-I want this one.
-Go ahead.

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.710
We're counting on you guys.

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:55.720
Yes. Is this as predicted as well?

00:16:56.840 --> 00:17:00.100
Then I'll make preparations so the mission
can be finalized at any time.

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:03.390
Right. And the people of Shibuya?

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:07.100
But that would be too...

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:10.150
It can't be helped
that half of them would be sacrificed?

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:11.860
What do you mean by "sacrificed"?

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:14.320
-Daisuke!
-"It can't be helped"?

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:16.820
-You're only going to save half of us?
-Hold on!

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:17.820
Milo!

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:19.950
Are you really on our side?

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:25.040
I want you to believe me.
That's all I can tell you right now.

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:26.750
Fine.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:28.250
I'll believe you.

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:30.460
And I will protect everyone!

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:37.800
Looks like they're here.

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:42.430
You said you were going to hand over
the AHRV agent, as well.

00:17:42.520 --> 00:17:45.480
We've brought the String Puppets
as promised.

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:47.650
The returnees
are being transported here now as well.

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:51.110
-And the AHRV agent?
-She should be arriving shortly!

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:54.030
<i>You don't have everything as promised.</i>

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:56.530
<i>Please wait!</i>
<i>They'll definitely bring her.</i>

00:17:56.610 --> 00:18:00.200
<i>You'll send back the people</i>
<i>on the list as promised, right?</i>

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:02.030
<i>-I'm going back, right?</i>
-As I thought.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:06.000
We will check the AHRV weapons first.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:13.090
This is so high!

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:15.170
I knew this would happen.

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:18.840
Lu and I will take care
of the enemies here.

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:21.390
-Marimari, go protect the buses!
-Got it!

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:25.600
You have chosen to resist us!

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:27.180
No, we didn't!

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:29.770
What's going on? Hurry and make them stop!

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:33.440
Muta!

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:37.610
For the charge of assisting the enemy,
you're under arrest!

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:45.620
Stay away from me!

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:52.920
Something has appeared!

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.840
Keisaku! Where are you?

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:57.800
What's going on?

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:09.140
Thanks!

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:11.020
Marimari!

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:12.860
Good job!

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:13.940
Daisuke!

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:19.070
You can leave the rest to me!

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:22.280
Help!

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:24.740
No!

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:40.010
-Why, you!
-Wait, Lu!

00:19:40.090 --> 00:19:44.010
We can't let them split up our firepower.
Let's return to Marimari!

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:51.520
We need to make adjustments
to collect the materials.

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.060
They have no love for mankind.

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:56.400
They're just a bunch of egoists.

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:30.660
Right. It appears
about 100 of our people were taken.

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:34.460
Among them was Daisuke's uncle
and Keisaku's mother.

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:41.210
Daisuke.

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:47.930
What's with the change in attitude?

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:50.390
You did well today, Daisuke.

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:00.440
I have something to report.

00:22:00.940 --> 00:22:04.820
Just now, I was given the mission
to save you in 2010.

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:07.240
So you are the Milo from that time.

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:09.280
I said the past is uncertain.

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:12.280
However, if going to save you in the past

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:14.200
results in this present,

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:16.500
I'll be glad for that.

00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:19.830
Whatever I may have said in the past,

00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:22.250
I'm sure it was what
our dead comrades and family

00:22:22.670 --> 00:22:23.960
wanted me to tell you.

00:22:24.050 --> 00:22:26.050
They entrusted those things to me.

00:22:26.970 --> 00:22:28.300
Excuse me.

00:22:28.760 --> 00:22:30.970
Thank you for saving us.

00:22:31.300 --> 00:22:33.720
-Thank you!
-You guys were cool!

00:22:34.770 --> 00:22:36.390
<i>It was a strange feeling.</i>

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:39.060
<i>Ever since that incident,</i>

00:22:39.520 --> 00:22:42.770
<i>all that I've wanted was there.</i>

00:22:43.690 --> 00:22:45.360
<i>Before I'd even realized it,</i>

00:22:45.530 --> 00:22:47.360
<i>I'd become like a hero!</i>

00:22:49.610 --> 00:22:51.910
Subtitle translation by Emily Noguchi
